# The web app's production Firebase config is a client-side web API key —
# Firebase's own security model makes these safe to expose publicly
# (real security is Firestore/Storage rules, not hiding this file), and the
# GitHub Actions build needs it checked in to build a working bundle at all.
!/packages/web/.env.production
# Firebase Functions v2 project-scoped env file — holds the Web Push VAPID
# private key. Every other sensitive credential in this repo lives in
# Secret Manager (see EMAIL_SECRETS in emailjs.service.ts); this one only
# uses a plain env file because the deploying service account currently
# lacks secretmanager.secrets.setIamPolicy (see deploy notes) — once that's
# granted, migrate VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY to a proper secret and delete this line.
/packages/backend/functions/.env.umoja-app
*.local
